    "description": "  Alerts and digest items must carry a short, useful preview of what the email\n  said so an operator can judge relevance without opening the mail\n  (sovereign-ai-bots #102, shipped in PR #116). The excerpt is a 2–5 line /\n  ≤320-char quote copied onto the alert at scan time from the LOCAL message\n  snippet only — never a remote fetch — and a \"signal chip\" names the matched\n  reasons in words (top-3, \"+N more\"). Both render into the Matrix message as a\n  quoted block and a \"Signals:\" line, and both omit cleanly when absent.\n\n  These scenarios drive real business emails through the live mailbox and assert\n  the three acceptance criteria end-to-end against the node:\n    - Every RED alert carries a short useful preview when available.\n    - Digest items include enough context (excerpt + signal chip) to judge\n      importance without opening the mail.\n    - The preview respects privacy / local-first: it is derived solely from the\n      locally stored snippet, capped, and contains no external content.",
